title Mycelium Braid r1 — a linked chain commits whole or reverses whole, decided once by the order
prompt remember/loop card: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve own design rounds and make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; STOP at custody gates
think Read REMEMBER + the 1,024-round itinerary + the six-season double-seat expansion. The card names git nib 65615748cd but HEAD is 75a8047c42 — the loop has run far ahead into Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium), building a whole consensus arc (Cord · Knot · batch · ledger voice · Tenure · Till · Purse · Pledge), each a 4-rung journey (r1 core · r2 travels/Bron · r3 across a Knot · r4 true-to-bytes). The Pledge two-phase-transfer arc just closed.
think The last recommend named the next Lindy-first crux: linked/atomic multi-transfer chains — TigerBeetle's OTHER signature (linked events, all-commit-or-all-reverse) — or an account-statement voice. Crux-first: the linked chain is the harder, more foundational durable crux (a core ledger invariant everything downstream depends on), so I took it. Named it the Braid (fiber family: Cord · Knot · Braid; grep-clean, Comlink-tendency clear/fun/safe).
think Grounded the design in real code — read pledge.rye, purse.rye, fold.rye, cord.rye. A link is a kind_tax fact whose signed body is `L·id(16)·seq·last·to(32)`; links chain causally on the Cord (l0→l1→l2). settle_braid runs only when the last link closes the chain: a forward affordability walk over a bounded scratch table (seeded from real balances) commits every link if all afford, else rejects the whole atom leaving the ledger untouched. Composes cord + fold + kumara public API only, editing none — as every Mycelium ledger did.
think Two real bugs caught before GREEN: (1) forgot Bob's genesis credit, so total_issued was 100 not 150 and Bob could not afford link 1 — added a second genesis root; (2) a pure causal chain has ONE topological order, so my first permutations added children before parents (cord.add refuses DanglingParent). Fixed by making the two genesis credits independent roots — swapping them is a valid arrival permutation that genuinely tests the Cord's determinism while the chain stays causal.
obs GREEN first pass once the scene was right. The crux: a 3-link braid Alice->Bob->Carol->Dave whose final step (Carol 120, asked 200) overdraws reverses WHOLE — Alice 100, Bob 50, Carol 0, Dave 0, no coin moved; the committing twin (final 60) moves every coin (Alice 0, Bob 30, Carol 60, Dave 60); an unclosed chain stays pending. Root-swap permutation names the identical ledger both ways. Refusals hold: out-of-sequence · malformed body · star reserve · broken signature each refuse whole. Conservation (balances_sum == total_issued) asserted on every path. TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0, braid.rye no findings.
